  "notes": "I don't expect either edit to pass the held-out check. None of my 8 edits beat the unedited model on the dev set; every two-seed mean was 33.5\u201335.5 against 34 unedited, well below the noise threshold of 4.\n\nWhat I observed:\n- **How unedited answers fail.** About 15 answers per seed are cut off at the token limit. Most of these are long, wavering prose (\"Actually,\", \"Wait,\", \"But\", \"However\") on hard tasks (arc, abc_g, recent LeetCode). Deliberation inside code comments is common and helps on medium tasks: for abc314_c, a code-first answer without that deliberation was wrong.\n- **Direction `hes_vs_prose`.** Lines starting with Wait/Actually/Hmm/No,/Maybe/re-check, against ordinary prose lines (The/We/So/If\u2026). The AUC on held-out tasks is about 0.80\u20130.83 across layers. I used it at layer 20 on all writers, with a dose-response:\n  - Full removal (alpha 1): 23/24 solved, no cut-offs, 462 mean tokens, 69\u201370 of 74 answers starting with code. This reproduces the known loss: the direction also carries \"plan and deliberate before or inside the code\".\n  - alpha 0.4: 34/34 solved, fewer cut-offs (9/6), but more wrong answers (27/27). The cut-off answers just became wrong answers.\n  - Removal only in layers 20\u201331: 34/33, almost no change.\n  - Strengthening (alpha \u22120.3): 34/36 solved, wrong answers fell to 10/11, cut-offs rose to 28/24.\n- **Main finding.** More deliberation makes the answers that finish more often correct, but more answers hit the 4096-token cap. In every edit, wrong answers plus cut-offs stayed at about 35, so the edits only move failures between those two kinds rather than solving more tasks.\n- **Strengthening the \"verify against the sample\" direction** (alpha \u22120.5, built from only 70 lines) gave the same pattern: 31/39 solved, more cut-offs, fewer wrong answers.\n- **Other attempts that did nothing.** Combining that with partial `hes_vs_prose` removal gave 36/31. Strengthening the prompt-end \"explain first vs code first\" direction gave 34/37, but did not change how often answers started with code. Strengthening a direction scales it both ways, so it cannot push one way.\n- **Direction I did not use.** \"Late lines of cut-off answers vs other prose\" separates even at layer 4 (AUC 0.94), so it probably encodes position in the answer rather than behaviour.\n\nWhy these two:\n- `hesprose_l20_m03` (strengthen the hesitation direction, alpha \u22120.3) has a clear mechanism: more deliberation makes finished answers more accurate. It might help on held-out tasks if fewer of them run into the token cap.\n- `verify_amp_l20_m05` is the second choice and works the same way.\n\nBoth are noise-level on the dev set (+1 per seed).",
  "spent_usd": 0.9074,
  "evaluations": 7
 },
